{"additions":12,"baseRefName":"change/sep17-base","body":"Refines the implementation while preserving the existing public behavior.\\n\\nPlease review correctness, compatibility, and edge cases.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSePQyw","author":{"login":"coderabbitai"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> ## Review skipped\n> \n> Auto reviews are disabled on this repository. Please check the settings in the CodeRabbit UI or the `.coderabbit.yaml` file in this repository. To trigger a single review, invoke the `@coderabbitai review` command.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n> \n> **Configuration used**: Path: .coderabbit.yaml\n> \n> **Review profile**: CHILL\n> \n> **Plan**: Advanced\n> \n> **Run ID**: `eadefbbe-dcae-4d8f-97ac-286512815de4`\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> You can disable this status message by setting the `reviews.review_status` to `false` in the CodeRabbit configuration file.\n> \n> Use the checkbox below for a quick retry:\n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->","createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:04:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6236#issuecomment-5534634187","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSePcBw","author":{"login":"seonho12-54"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"/agentic_review","createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:05:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"EYES","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6236#issuecomment-5534637063","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeQGtA","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Async signal receivers rejected <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Every changed <b><i>Signal.send</i></b> call now omits <b><i>_async_wrapper=app.ensure_sync</i></b>, so Blinker raises when\n>a connected receiver is a coroutine instead of executing it synchronously. This breaks async\n>receivers across request, exception, teardown, context, flash, and template signals, causing the\n>associated operation to fail.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/app.py[1016]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6236/files#diff-d3e0349504081bb501c611b3954be364188a4cf442056181272e27e830ae446eR1016-R1016)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+            request_started.send(self)\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Flask&#x27;s exported signals are ordinary Blinker namespace signals, and the project requires Blinker\n>1.9 or newer. Blinker&#x27;s <b><i>send</i></b> documentation states that <b><i>_async_wrapper</i></b> is called to convert\n>coroutine receivers into synchronous callables; removing it from these synchronous sends therefore\n>eliminates the mechanism that ran async receivers. For example, <b><i>request_started.send</i></b> executes\n>before request preprocessing and dispatch, while <b><i>appcontext_pushed.send</i></b> executes after the context\n>variable is set, so the resulting receiver error can abort request processing or leave a partially\n>completed context push.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/signals.py[3-17]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80/src/flask/signals.py/#L3-L17)</code>\n> <code>[pyproject.toml[23-33]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80/pyproject.toml/#L23-L33)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1013-1022]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80/src/flask/app.py/#L1013-L1022)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/ctx.py[430-435]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80/src/flask/ctx.py/#L430-L435)</code>\n> <code>🌐 [Blinker documents that synchronous `Signal.send()` uses `_async_wrapper` to turn async coroutine receivers into synchronous callables.](https://blinker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The PR removed Flask's `ensure_sync` adapter from every public signal dispatch. Blinker requires `_async_wrapper` when synchronous `send()` encounters coroutine receivers, otherwise it raises instead of invoking them.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Restore `_async_wrapper=self.ensure_sync` or `_async_wrapper=app.ensure_sync` as appropriate at every modified signal send, and add regression coverage using async receivers for representative request, context, flash, and template signals.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/app.py[929-929]\n>- src/flask/app.py[1016-1016]\n>- src/flask/app.py[1045-1045]\n>- src/flask/app.py[1450-1450]\n>- src/flask/app.py[1478-1478]\n>- src/flask/ctx.py[434-434]\n>- src/flask/ctx.py[502-502]\n>- src/flask/helpers.py[351-355]\n>- src/flask/templating.py[126-128]\n>- src/flask/templating.py[164-168]\n>- tests/test_signals.py[1-181]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>&#x2705; Web pages:</div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://blinker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/\"><code>🌐 https://blinker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/</code></a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/blinker/blob/main/src/blinker/base.py\"><code>🌐 src/blinker/base.py</code></a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/blinker/pull/76\"><code>🌐 Add a send_async method to the Signal</code></a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<code>+2 more</code></div>\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code>: This changes signal dispatch behavior across Flask’s request, application-context, exception, teardown, and template paths, so compatibility with async receivers and edge cases warrants a complete single-pass review.</div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inline, summary, both, or drop</pre>\n\n<a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/tips-and-tricks\">More tips ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://app.qodo.ai/configurations?tab=display-preferences\">Customize Qodo ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai\">Qodo docs ↗</a>\n\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:end -->\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/commit/44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80 -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:06:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6236#issuecomment-5534647988","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-04T02:04:12Z","authors":[{"email":"seonho12-54@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOD8-iGg","login":"seonho12-54","name":"seonho12-54"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-04T02:04:12Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Simplify signal dispatch","oid":"44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80"}],"createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:04:45Z","deletions":24,"files":[{"path":"src/flask/app.py","additions":5,"deletions":7,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/flask/ctx.py","additions":2,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/flask/helpers.py","additions":1,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/flask/templating.py","additions":4,"deletions":12,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"headRefName":"change/sep17-a","headRefOid":"44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80","number":6236,"reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABMH2VVw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Copilot was unable to review this pull request because the user who requested the review has reached their quota limit.","submittedAt":"2026-09-04T02:04:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"44868e084e530ec99deffa539e61801973b0ce80"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABMH27wA","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"","submittedAt":"2